 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? The seat tube will have a gap as you flip it from right to left. Is it wide enough to push the seat post in by a few inches? Then it' probably the right height. A few more turns with your weight on it should lock it in place. No worries. Then lift yourself off the pedals and push down. That's the point at which you can pedal without lifting. The seat should be lower than that. Probably, but you'll be perched like an eagle. A lower seat is worth it for being able to touch both pedals at the top.",
